;; Written by Claude, 2026-10-16, for Phase 17 step 5
;; (doc/developer/vms-sdl-interfaces.md, part 7, proposal 2, approved by
;; the user); reviewed by the user, 2026-10-16. It replaces the file the user
;; reviewed on 2026-10-15. Why this is right:
;; - Only VmsArguments' key (the .EXTERNAL POC_K1_) changes, since its
;;   interface gained ArrayDescriptor and DescribeArray; this program
;;   does not use them.
;; As the user reviewed it on 2026-10-15:
;; - length, which SetItem takes as its returnLength, is now a
;;   SYSTEM.CARD16, as VmsArguments' is (its comment in the variables'
;;   list says so); the source keeps its lines, so no line number moves.
;; - VmsArguments' key (the .EXTERNAL POC_K1_) is new, as its interface
;;   changed.
;; The rest is as the user reviewed it on 2026-10-14:
;; - Each argument list is CALLG's, one longword an argument (the count
;;   first), as for any external; nothing else is pushed.
;; - By value (PassValues): BOOLEAN and CHAR zero-extended (MOVZBL),
;;   SHORTINT and INTEGER sign-extended (CVTBL, CVTWL), a REAL as its
;;   F_floating longword (MOVF), a SET, an address; a procedure its entry
;;   mask's address (MOVAB), NIL 0 (CLRL).
;; - VAR (PassVars): the variable's address (MOVAB), a VAR parameter's
;;   own (MOVL 4(AP)); an open array, a VAR one included, element 0's
;;   address alone, with no lengths after it (5 arguments for 5
;;   parameters); NIL 0.
;; - Read only (PassReadOnly): a variable of the formal's own type by its
;;   address (status, huge, long, items, short); a structured constant
;;   (L_CONST_1) and a string constant (L_STR_1, padded to the formal's 8
;;   bytes) from POC_CONST; anything else copied to a temporary in the
;;   frame first, converted to the formal's type (CVTWL from an INTEGER,
;;   CVTFG from a REAL, a HUGEINT constant's two halves, status * 2,
;;   huge + 1), and the temporary's address passed. The temporaries'
;;   slots are kept until CALLG returns. A value open array parameter
;;   passes the address of its copy (MOVL -4(FP)). NIL 0.
;; - An open ARRAY OF CHAR (PassStrings), whatever its mode: an 8-byte
;;   CLASS_S descriptor in the frame - its length word, then
;;   DSC$K_DTYPE_T 14 and DSC$K_CLASS_S 1 as one word (#^X010E), then the
;;   address - and the descriptor's address in the list (MOVAQ). A
;;   constant is described at its own length (8 for "constant", 1 for
;;   "x"); a fixed array at its length (#32); an open array at its length
;;   from the argument list, cut to 65,535 (CMPL, BLEQU, MOVW #65535).
;;   An input (a value or read-only parameter) is then shortened to its
;;   first 0X: LOCC #0 over the descriptor's length and address leaves in
;;   R0 the bytes from the 0X to the end, 0 if there is none, and SUBW2
;;   R0 takes them off. An output (VAR) is described whole. NIL 0.
;; - A result narrower than a longword (NarrowResults) is widened by the
;;   caller from R0's low byte or word (CVTBL, CVTBW, CVTWL), never read
;;   as a longword, since the calling standard leaves R0's high bits
;;   undefined (2.4); a BOOLEAN's low bit is tested (BLBS).
;; - A read-only ARRAY OF SYSTEM.BYTE (PassBytes; part 2, proposal 7,
;;   added and reviewed by the user 2026-10-14) takes any actual: a variable of any
;;   type by its own address (huge, item, name, status); a value copied to
;;   a temporary in the frame first, in its own type (huge + 1's quadword,
;;   the constant's longword, real * 2.0's F_floating), and the
;;   temporary's address passed; a string constant (L_STR_5) and a
;;   structured one (L_CONST_1) from POC_CONST; NIL 0.
